EXT. SOAPBOX DERBY PIT LANE - DAY

Hot asphalt and hay bales. A hand-painted cart, number 7, rests on its wheels at the starting ramp. Banners snap in the wind.

COACH BRONWEN MAYHEW (50s, whistle, sun visor) crouches at the cart's front axle with a wrench, tightening a nut while shouting over her shoulder. TEODORO "TEDDY" LACROIX (12, helmet too large, goggles pushed up) kneels in the cockpit, adjusting the steering rope, then stops to wave at someone in the crowd, then goes back to the rope. A loudspeaker on a pole crackles above them.

RACE CONTROL (V.O.)
(over loudspeaker)
Car seven to the line. Car seven, two minutes.

BRONWEN
I heard.

TEDDY
Did they say two minutes?

BRONWEN
They said two minutes.

TEDDY
Is it two or one-thirty?

RACE CONTROL (V.O.)
(over loudspeaker)
Car seven, you are blocking the ramp.

BRONWEN
(to the sky)
We're not blocking, we're tuning!

TEDDY
Coach, the left wheel is wobbling.

BRONWEN
It's not wobbling, it's thinking.

RACE CONTROL (V.O.)
(over loudspeaker)
One minute thirty.

Bronwen drops the wrench, tugs Teddy's chin strap tight, slaps the helmet twice, and pushes the cart up the ramp with both hands. Teddy drops his goggles and grips the rope.

TEDDY
Coach.

BRONWEN
Don't speak. Steer.
